{:edb/db-before-t 2112 :edb/db-after-t 2113 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535425 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:49:11.403Z" 13194139535425 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348594 13194139535425 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348601 13194139535425 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348608 13194139535425 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348611 13194139535425 true] [17592186348594 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348595 13194139535425 true] [17592186348594 1089 "q-128461" 13194139535425 true] [17592186348594 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535425 true] [17592186348594 1100 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨{k}^{2},7,4⟩,$ $b=⟨6,7,4⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,0,2⟩$ are coplanar." 13194139535425 true] [17592186348594 1113 #uuid "41e53fe4-b06e-5150-a976-5badf29f5d4c" 13194139535425 true] [17592186348594 1145 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2} & 7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={k}^{2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={k}^{2}(7\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 4)-7(6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4)+4(6\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 7) \\\\  & =14{k}^{2}+0-84 \\\\  & =14{k}^{2}-84 \\\\  & =14({k}^{2}-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 14({k}^{2}-6) & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =6 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\sqrt{6}$ or $k=\\sqrt{6}.$" 13194139535425 true] [17592186348595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348596 13194139535425 true] [17592186348595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348597 13194139535425 true] [17592186348595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348598 13194139535425 true] [17592186348595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348599 13194139535425 true] [17592186348595 1000 #edb/ref 1759218